{{Codex|Narin's signature bow is the north wind's icy messenger. Alt Fire unleashes a charged blizzard arrow that freezes enemies it touches and leaves behind a chilling path.}}
'''Nunchasa''' is {{WF|Narin|Narin's}} [[Signature Weapon|signature]] bow. Attacking enemies builds charges to use the [[Alternate Fire]]: a charged wide {{D|Cold}} projectile.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals {{D|Cold}} and {{D|Puncture}} damage on its primary fire and primarily {{D|Cold}} damage on its [[Alternate Fire]].
*Hits on enemies build up alt-fire charges, represented by five icicles around the lower portion of the reticle, each being split in half. '''5''' charges are needed to fully charge the alt-fire, with direct hits generating half a charge and [[Enemy Body Parts|weak point]] hits one charge.
**Hits created through [[Multishot]], and [[Punch Through]] contribute to charging the Alt-fire. Additionally, {{D|Blast}} status effects grant charge, but not upon their death detonation. [[Extra Hit]] effects (such as {{A|Toxic Lash}}) do not grant extra charge.
**Alt-fire unleashes a '''2''' meter wide projectile with infinite body [[Punch Through]] and forced {{D|Cold|Freeze}} on enemies caught within the radius, while leaving behind a trail that inflicts '''1''' {{D|Cold}} proc per second on enemies that walk into it.
***Trail lasts for 10 seconds.
***Has a [[Enemy Body Parts|headshot]] multiplier of 1x.
***Projectile and trail width is unaffected by {{M|Firestorm}} ({{M|Primed Firestorm|Primed}}).
*Two innate {{Pol|V}} polarities.
{{Advantages|
}}

{{Disadvantages|
}}

==Acquisition==
Nunchasa's blueprints can be purchased from [[Cephalon Melica]] on [[Yuvan Peak]], [[Earth]], or the [[Chrysalith]], [[Zariman Ten Zero]], for {{Resource|Entropic Kuva}}, which are dropped by [[Entropic Eximus]] in the Zariman.

The main blueprint costs {{Resource|Entropic Kuva|200}}, while the limb, grip, and string blueprints cost {{Resource|Entropic Kuva|50}} each, requiring {{Resource|Entropic Kuva|400}} total.

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Notes==
* Similar to {{Weapon|Nataruk}}, cannot equip {{M|Split Flights}}.

==Trivia==
* Nunchasa is portmanteau of Nun (눈), Korean word for snow, and Chasa (차사), a temporary position created for important task.
** Chasa likely refers to Hamheung Chasa (함흥차사), an idiom that tells a story of Chasas getting sent to Hamheung to recover the royal seal from the previous king, but end up getting killed by him, who shot them with his bow. Though the story is widely known, it is not based on historical facts.

